          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Objective\nCreate an implementation guide from a specification document.\n**DO NOT do the work.** ONLY produce the implementation guide as defined below.\n\n## Requirements\n- If docs/plans/ISS-59_m4_anthropic_streaming_spec.md is empty or omitted, pull the latest `*_spec.md` from `docs/plans/` and verify it with the user.\n- Read the spec's **Context & Constraints** before writing tasks. Do not re-derive or re-evaluate decisions already made there.\n- Each task must reference the exact file path and function/method (e.g. `internal/handler/auth.go: UpdateUser()`).\n- Each task must be implementable and testable in isolation.\n- Tasks ordered by dependency and priority.\n- If anything is unclear, ask — then update the spec to match.\n- Specifiy which parts of the implementation checklist can be done in parallel.\n- Place the file in `docs/plans/` with the name `xxx_nnn_implement.md`\n  - \"xxx\" = linear id matching the spec file\n  - \"nnn\" = task to achieve\n\n## Testing Rules\n- Test real code, not mocks. If deleting the code under test doesn't break the test, the test adds no value.\n- Mock at the router level only for auth gating, input validation, and error propagation.\n\n## Document Structure\n\n### Section 1: Context Summary\nOne paragraph summarizing the *why* behind this implementation, drawn from the spec's Context & Constraints. Anchors the executing agent without needing to re-read the spec.\n\n### Section 2: Implementation Checklist\n- `- [ ] {Task description}` format\n- Exact file path and function/method on each task\n- Include test tasks alongside implementation tasks",
